They even threw in the Intel RK 770 for funsies.

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:02.860
Now, 1080p performance in rasterized games

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:04.880
might seem kind of irrelevant

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:07.600
for an enthusiast tier GPU these days,

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:09.520
but for many competitive gamers,

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:12.040
high frame rates are way more important

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:13.480
than high resolution.

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:17.440
And if you're one of them, the RTX 4070 is proper quick

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:21.920
with performance landing within 2% of the RTX 3080.

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:24.060
This might not be the leap forward

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:25.240
that you were hoping for,

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:28.960
but given the pricing of even secondhand 3080s,

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:33.960
it's kind of looking like a W, kind of, give me a sec.

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:36.660
At 1440p, the story remains the same

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:40.680
with the 4070 neck and neck with the RTX 3080.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:43.160
But what really stood out to us here

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:44.780
at both of these resolutions

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:48.560
is how flipping fast AMD's last gen has gotten

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:50.900
thanks to their ongoing software updates.

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:55.900
The 6800 XT now enjoys a small lead over the 3080

00:02:56.360 --> 00:03:00.440
with the 7900 XT coming in a whole 40% faster

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:04.880
than the 4070 and nearly matching the RTX 4080,

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:07.680
a GPU that costs $400 more.

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:12.680
Then at 4K, the 4070s W gets even more twisted and complex

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:15.280
because outside of Forza,

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:18.160
the RTX 3080 ends up outrunning it

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:22.520
by anywhere from five to 19%,

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:25.400
or at least it does until you turn on ray tracing

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:27.760
where the gap narrows significantly.

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:30.160
Now the story Nvidia wants to focus on here

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:35.160
is not how the 4070 beats last gen by 25 to 30%,

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:40.520
but rather on how it convincingly destroys the GTX 1080.

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:42.160
From my point of view though,

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:43.700
beating a seven-year-old card

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:46.640
is not the most incredible of feats,

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:48.160
unless your name is Intel.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:50.500
It's just obvious that Nvidia is bringing this up

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:52.640
because they recognize the generation

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:55.240
over generation upgrade is not that big

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:58.160
and they hope that it's all you Pascal owners out there

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:00.880
that are finally gonna bite the bullet and upgrade.

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:02.140
Moving on to productivity.

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:04.880
In our benchmarks, there was one standout.

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:09.380
In Photoshop, the Intel ARC A770 was able to best

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:13.160
not only the 4070, but also the 4070 Ti

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:16.440
and was even within spinning distance of the RTX 4080.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:18.160
I mean, I'm not sure that the average user

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:20.080
updating their Tinder profile is gonna notice,

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:23.520
but whatever hardware acceleration Intel built for ARC

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:25.140
definitely works.

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:26.760
Then outside of Photoshop,

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:29.360
ARC returns to its rightful place at the bottom of the stack

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:32.280
and the rest of the story remains largely the same as gaming

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:35.660
with the RTX 3080 and 4070 trading places

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:37.320
depending on the exact workload

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:39.480
and AMD once again showing off

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:42.700
that fine line driver development.

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:45.480
Outside of Blender, which remains a sore spot for Team Red,

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:48.240
the 6800 XT put on an amazing show

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:52.280
winning more titles than it lost at a lower price.

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:55.640
So if we're looking at the performance of an RTX 3080,

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:58.800
but at the price of an RTX 3070 Ti,

00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:01.140
given how crap GPU prices have been

00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:04.800
for the last couple of years, this is great, right?

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:09.800
Well, yes, but saying an RTX 4070 for $600

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:14.040
is better than an RTX 3080 for like, what did it peak at?

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:16.320
$1,600 or something like that?

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:18.640
That's like saying that a paddle to the ass

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:21.400
is better than a slap to the face.

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:23.760
Both can be fun when the kids are out of town

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:26.360
and we do have matching couples undies on lttstore.com

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:28.120
by the way to make this even more awkward,

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:29.440
but none of that is the point.

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:33.120
The point is that when compared to last gen, sure,

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:37.300
Nvidia gave us a solid increase in performance,

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:41.680
but they also gave us an equally solid increase in price

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:44.160
and this is the second time in two generations

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:45.920
that they've pulled this move.

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:49.240
When we went from the 1000 series to the 2000 series,

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:50.560
they did the same thing.

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:52.640
We got a nearly proportional increase

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:56.160
in both price and performance with Nvidia hoarding

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:58.240
the benefits of their new architecture

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:00.400
and using them to line their own pockets

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:03.080
rather than passing them along to the consumer.

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:05.200
You see, the industry norm has been

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:08.200
that as our manufacturing technology improves,

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:12.600
the same amount of compute becomes less expensive.

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:13.440
In this case,

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:16.360
Nvidia went from Samsung's eight nanometer node

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:18.600
to TSMC and five.

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:21.480
That's how they packed the same number of CUDA cores

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:24.680
into just 295 millimeters squared

00:06:24.680 --> 00:06:28.700
compared to the 392 millimeter squared die of the 3070,

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:30.600
which is super cool,

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:34.200
but then if it supposedly didn't cost any less,

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:36.160
why the heck did they even bother?

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:38.100
Well, there are two reasons for that.

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:41.360
Efficiency and then probably more importantly,

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:43.400
the RTX 4090.

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:45.400
But let's talk efficiency first.

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:49.080
For the amount of performance that the RTX 4070 delivers,

00:06:49.080 --> 00:06:51.240
it sips power.

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:53.640
It has a TGP of 200 Watts,

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:56.400
but Nvidia says that the average gaming power draw

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:59.280
is more like 184 and in our testing,

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:01.080
that was basically bang on,

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:03.080
which is darn impressive given

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:05.440
that the performance comparable RTX 3080

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:09.960
drew an average of 296 Watts during the same test.

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:12.720
Also a good sign is that the maximum recorded wattage

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:15.880
of the 4070 was just 233 Watts

00:07:15.880 --> 00:07:19.420
compared to a whopping 412 for the 3080.

00:07:19.420 --> 00:07:20.920
So not only will you be saving money

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:22.100
on your monthly energy bill,

00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:24.480
but you also don't have to worry about a power spike

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:27.540
sending your aging power supply into the shadow realm.

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:29.200
Now you might be hoping that this means

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:31.540
there's a lot of headroom for overclocking,

00:07:31.540 --> 00:07:33.400
but sadly it looks like Nvidia

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:35.500
has really locked this card down

00:07:35.500 --> 00:07:37.760
and we weren't able to meaningfully improve performance

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:40.540
by tinkering with any of the knobs and dials.

00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:42.480
I don't think that this efficiency gain

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:45.620
is why Nvidia decided to go TSMC 5N though.

00:07:45.620 --> 00:07:48.280
And it might actually have been better for consumers

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:50.080
if they just took everything they learned

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:52.760
about the mature eight nanometer Samsung node

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:55.220
and then made better GPUs with it.

00:07:55.220 --> 00:07:57.280
Kind of like what they did back in 2014

00:07:57.280 --> 00:07:59.760
using the same 28 nanometer node

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:03.360
for both the GTX 770 and 970.

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:05.640
The issue though is if they had done that

00:08:05.640 --> 00:08:09.000
the RTX 4090 simply wouldn't have been feasible.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:10.820
It would have drawn too much power

00:08:10.820 --> 00:08:13.080
and it would have given AMD an opportunity

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:14.840
to have a competitive flagship

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:18.220
which would be utterly unacceptable.

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:20.340
The 4090 is a true generational leap

00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:23.760
coming in at just 7% more cost than the 3090

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:26.160
while being over 50% faster.

00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:29.040
So then why the heck isn't that true

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:31.360
of the rest of the lineup Nvidia?

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:34.040
Well, because from their point of view

00:08:34.040 --> 00:08:37.280
they did give you a generational performance leap

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:40.140
but through AI rather than raw grunt.

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:43.440
And in fairness, they aren't entirely wrong here.

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:46.280
By turning on DLSS3 frame generation

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:50.840
the RTX 4070 is able to easily dispatch the RTX 3080

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:55.520
and even deliver performance about on par with the 4080

00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:58.880
before its AI assistance is kicked in.

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:02.700
Now frame generation may increase input latency

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:05.840
but Nvidia Reflex does go a long way

00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:07.600
