00:10:14.120 --> 00:10:15.800
This is a really good product

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:16.760
but that doesn't mean

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:18.920
that we are unreservedly happy about it.

00:10:18.920 --> 00:10:22.720
Nvidia's whining about how they simply can't pass along

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:27.280
any silicon cost savings just doesn't hold a ton of water.

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:29.260
Development costs for new process nodes

00:10:29.260 --> 00:10:31.560
have increased substantially

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:35.120
but I also think that Nvidia does have some room to move here

00:10:35.120 --> 00:10:38.200
